    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0429" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 (E. W.)/11–742: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the War
                        Department </hi><anchor n="39" xml:id="d418-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1942-11-03T17:00:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1942-11-02T00:00:00-05:00">undated</date>.]<lb/>[Received
                        November 3, 1942—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 752. [From Murphy.] Your Mike 26, 1st [<hi rendition="#italic">31st</hi>]
                    Flagpole and Kingpin advised. Kingpin has already sent word that in event of <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Torch</hi> we should do everything to placate
                    Spaniards in order to avoid winter campaign in Riff thus losing time in march to
                    Tunisia. Kingpin would even favor offering territorial concession up to River
                    Ouergha but not as far as Sebaâ. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d418-f1" n="39" type="source" xml:id="d418-f1-content">
                <p>Copy supplied by the Office of the Secretary of Defense under cover of letter of
                    September 7, 1960.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
